Macro Behaviour on failure <code>REQUIRE(expr)</code> Stops current test immediately (like assert) <code>CHECK(expr)</code> Records failure but continues test execution <code>REQUIRE_FALSE(e)</code> Fails if expression is true; stops test <code>CHECK_FALSE(e)</code> Fails if expression is true; continues test <code>REQUIRE_THAT</code> Fail + stop, with a Matcher <code>CHECK_THAT</code> Fail + continue, with a Matcher <pre><code>// Use CHECK when you want to see ALL failures in one run:
CHECK(a.x == 1);
CHECK(a.y == 2);
CHECK(a.z == 3);

// Use REQUIRE when subsequent assertions make no sense after failure:
REQUIRE(ptr != nullptr);
REQUIRE(ptr-&gt;valid());   // only makes sense if ptr is not null
</code></pre>

